  "body": "## What changed\n\nGPU stock sim S1 (#2626). This PR adds a CPU f32 twin of the per-cell cut kernel and the brick work list. The change is additive. No caller changes, and the f64 kernel does not change.\n\n- `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/cut_twin.rs`: the f32 cell cut.\n  - Coordinates are relative to the tile. The tile is the brick (8 cells a side).\n  - The ball uses the capsule closed form. The upright flat uses the level closed form, the plunge closed form, or a 32-step golden section. This is the same order as `Sweep::dist` in f64.\n  - The kernel adds a margin to each distance before it claims a cell: `TWIN_ULPS` (32) f32 epsilons of the tile scale, plus `1e-6` of the path length on the flat path. Thus the twin never removes more than the f64 cut.\n  - `ordered_bits` / `from_ordered_bits` give the order-preserving u32 key. The max law runs on that key, which is the law of a GPU `atomicMax`.\n- `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/cut_twin_work.rs`: the brick work list and its CPU run.\n  - The window of each chord is the f64 `Sweep::window`, clipped to the `pack_cut` lattice. The items are sorted by brick, then by chord.\n  - `run_twin` writes the cut layer in the dense layout of `preview::pack_cut`, with the same `-4 cap` floor.\n  - The twin refuses by name: each tool other than the ball and the flat end mill, an arc, a tilted axis, a zero-length move, a non-finite value, a bad tool size, and a chord window above `TWIN_MAX_CELLS_PER_CHORD`.\n- `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/mod.rs`: the two modules and their exports.\n- `docs/decisions/2626-f32-cut-twin.md`: 8 decisions taken unattended.\n\n## Readings\n\n- One-sided parity on a 16 x 16 x 8 block (cell 0.7, cap 2.8), with a level feed, a ramp, a plunge, a diagonal ramp and a rapid.\n  - `twin <= f64` holds with no tolerance for each texel. The f64-to-f32 pack rounding keeps order.\n  - `twin >= f64 - tol`, with `tol = 96 * eps * 64 + 1e-4` (about 7.3e-4 mm). The test comment gives the reason for the bound.\n- The two values clamp at `-cap` before the compare. A cut below `-cap` never shows.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/sim/tests/stock_cut_twin.rs`:\n- `the_ball_twin_never_removes_more_than_the_f64_cut`\n- `the_flat_twin_never_removes_more_than_the_f64_cut`\n- `the_ordered_key_keeps_the_order_of_negative_zero_and_positive`\n- `the_batch_answers_bit_for_bit_in_any_move_order`\n- `the_work_list_covers_every_claimed_cell_inside_its_bricks`\n- `degenerate_input_refuses_with_a_clean_error`\n- `every_other_tool_refuses_by_name`\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) on head 65e391e04: 78 steps, 0 failed, not VOID. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- GPU and WGSL code. That is S2.\n- Arc moves, tilted poses and the other tools. The twin refuses them.\n- The ray-entry layers (`cut_ups`, `cut_downs`).\n- Lattices larger than the test fixture, and large world offsets.\n\n## Changelog\n\nChangelog: Stock simulation: an f32 CPU reference of the GPU cell cut and its brick work list (no user-visible change yet).\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2626\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
